    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) – a fruit (specifically a pomelo).\nWu and Shi (2022) notes that 由 was originally a component extracted from the oracle bone script of 柚 (“pomelo”), where it depicted the fruit itself. It was later used exclusively for phonetic loans, fully differentiating from 柚.\nTraditional analysis in Shuowen interprets it as a container with a needle (十, original form of 針). Alternatively, Tang Lan (唐蘭) interpreted it as the pictogram of a helmet (original character of 冑)."
    }
